 Melayu) is the earliest extant written history of Malaya for it is believed that the first version was composed only some twenty years after the capture of Malacca by the Portuguese when memories of former reigns were still fresh. The Annals is a most vivid and readable account of the greatness of Malacca. In addition we also have as sources the works of sixteenth-century Portuguese historians and some passing references in Chinese archives." "That first millennium CE Southeast Asians were also literate is suggested by Chinese emissaries who describe libraries of texts. Yet the indigenous historical tradition that we can now access consists largely of inscribed stelae that record dedications and elite donations to local shrines and ritual monuments."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 971, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 788})
